1. WHAT THIS IS

"The Software" means everything in this repository: source code, tests, scripts, configuration, design tokens,
documentation (including everything in docs/), text, and any other material, in any form, together with any copy
or part of it. The Software is the confidential and proprietary intellectual property of Team 610.

The Software is NOT open source. Nothing in this license, in the repository's visibility on any website, or in
any other conduct of Team 610 grants you rights that are not written in this license.

2. WHO MAY USE IT, AND HOW

2.1  Team members. Current members and mentors of Team 610, while they are members, may use, run and modify the
     Software on devices and accounts controlled by the team, solely for Team 610's scouting and strategy work
     and for the team's own training of its members.

2.2  Reading for education. Anyone else who lawfully has access to the Software may read it, in place, for their
     own private education. This permission covers reading and learning from it. It does not cover anything
     listed in section 3.

2.3  Nothing else. Every right not granted in 2.1 or 2.2 is reserved by Team 610.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

Unless Team 610 has given you written permission signed by a mentor or officer of the team, you may not:

 (a) copy, reproduce, download for retention, mirror, fork, clone for any purpose other than reading under 2.2,
     or archive the Software, in whole or in part;
 (b) modify it, translate it, adapt it, port it to another language or framework, or create derivative works,
     including works that closely follow its structure, design, algorithms, data model or documentation;
 (c) distribute, publish, sublicense, sell, rent, lend, host or make it available to any third party, including
     as a service;
 (d) run it for any team, event, organisation or purpose other than those in 2.1;
 (e) use it, or any part of it, to train, fine-tune, evaluate or prompt a machine-learning or AI model, or to
     build a dataset for one, except that members of Team 610 may use AI coding assistants on the Software
     while working on it for the team, and that does not allow the assistant's provider to retain or train on it
     beyond what the team's agreement with that provider already allows;
 (f) remove, hide or alter any copyright, license or ownership notice;
 (g) use Team 610's name, number, logos or the names of its members to suggest endorsement of anything else;
 (h) try to extract, discover or publish any secret, credential, private data or non-public design it contains.

